{
    "background_story": "Sariah was a brilliant biomedical engineer who had always been fascinated by the human body's intricacies. Growing up, she watched her grandmother struggle with chronic respiratory issues, which sparked her interest in developing innovative medical devices. Sariah's breakthrough came when she created a wearable oximeter that could track oxygen levels in real-time, providing crucial data for patients with respiratory conditions. Her device, dubbed 'OxiCare,' was met with widespread acclaim and quickly became a staple in hospitals worldwide. Sariah's invention not only improved patient outcomes but also brought her closer to her grandmother, who was one of the first beneficiaries of OxiCare. As Sariah continued to refine her design, she remained committed to making healthcare more accessible and affordable, inspired by the impact her work had on those she loved.",
